{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs on it, including those that need","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge storage.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A grid is numbered row-major."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-closure","type":"heading","text":"The closure"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"successors(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", once per edge, as any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as an array or a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list. A specialized","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"build inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once. ","type":"text"},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"outDegree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call it once each, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per vertex.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex. This is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not checked, and a closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm. Each target is checked to be a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and yields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them by count. A "},{"code":"lazy.filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls its predicate per element and carries the unfiltered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator’s state, which costs more per edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Positions","type":"heading","text":"Positions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":", which holds its source, its rank in the source’s row, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"type":"text","text":", which is unique even among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges and self-loops. Because the position carries the target, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a weight closure reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge indices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Attached-values","type":"heading","text":"Attached values"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is not a "},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because "},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has a dense offset only after every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier row is counted. Keep vertex values in an array of "},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" indexed by vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compute edge values from the position ("},{"code":"$0.source","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", because a closure has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documenta